  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:5542",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is implicated in the activation of OAW-42 through a multi-step pathway involving purinoceptor signaling. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin targets P2X purinoceptor 1, which is subsequently inhibited by Mollicellin N, and both of these molecules are involved in the regulation of OAW-42. Similarly, doxorubicin also targets COLO-792 and NCI-H46, which in turn are linked to the same target molecule, 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which also targets OAW-42. This indicates that doxorubicin may exert its effects on OAW-42 through a common downstream pathway, possibly involving the activation of purinoceptors or the modulation of a shared metabolic or signaling molecule. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which doxorubicin influences OAW-42, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
